-- Write epoch for the working-set apply (PR1 of the trusted-novelty series).
--
-- Why this exists: the apply path bulk-probes every id the content spine already
-- claimed novel, because a concurrent writer may have landed overlapping rows
-- between the unlocked descent and the apply transaction. That probe is the
-- guard, not the common case — on a quiet substrate nothing intervened and the
-- probe re-proves absence the descent already knew. A monotonic DB-side write
-- epoch makes "nothing intervened" PROVABLE: every write-lane transaction calls
-- nextval BEFORE writing, so an apply that recorded last_value after its own
-- commit and reads the same value at its next verify has witnessed every
-- write-lane transaction in between (its own bumps subtracted) and knows no
-- foreign writer touched the substrate.
--
-- THIS PR ONLY INTRODUCES THE EPOCH AND ITS TELEMETRY. Writers bump it and log
-- the per-apply foreign delta so live seeds quantify how often the trust
-- condition would hold; no probe/skip decision reads it yet.
--
-- Semantics:
--   * Every write-lane transaction (apply control tx, parallel COPY sub-tx,
--     attestation merge sub-tx, consensus fold segment, highway-mask deposit)
--     calls nextval BEFORE its writes.
--   * Sequence advances survive rollback and crash. That is the CONSERVATIVE
--     direction: an aborted write still moves the epoch, so the next apply sees
--     a foreign delta and re-probes — a false "someone wrote" costs one probe;
--     a rewinding epoch could hide a committed foreign write behind an equal
--     reading, which would be fatal to a future probe skip.
--   * CACHE 1, explicitly: per-session value caching would let a writer's bump
--     land out of order with its writes as observed by another session's
--     last_value read, and the foreign-delta arithmetic (delta = calls made)
--     only holds when every nextval is a single uncached increment.
--
-- Older installed extensions lack this sequence; writers probe to_regclass once
-- and degrade to always-probing. Grants match sibling schema objects: none
-- beyond the extension schema's own — the write lane connects as the
-- installing role.
CREATE SEQUENCE IF NOT EXISTS apply_write_epoch CACHE 1;

COMMENT ON SEQUENCE apply_write_epoch IS
    'Laplace: monotonic write-lane epoch. Every write-lane transaction calls '
    'nextval before writing; an unchanged last_value across a window proves no '
    'writer intervened. Advances survive rollback (conservative: aborted writes '
    'still force the next apply to re-probe).';
